{"term":"Liebesnest","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"sex_work_pornography","subcategory":"tryst_location","concept":"love_affair","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"euphemism","crude":15,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":87,"recognition_pct_peak":90,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"'Love nest'; a private, often secret, place — typically a rented room or apartment — used by a couple for illicit or discreet sexual encounters.","english_term":"love nest","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Primarily implies secrecy and extramarital infidelity rather than commercial sex; the English calque 'love nest' is a near-exact translation; mapped to love_affair because no registry concept covers a physical venue for illicit trysts."}
{"term":"Nutte","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"sex_work_pornography","subcategory":"sex_worker_slur","concept":"sex_worker","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":75,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":97,"recognition_pct_peak":97,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Crude slang for a prostitute; also widely deployed as a general pejorative insult for any sexually immoral or promiscuous woman.","english_term":"hooker","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"One of the most common crude terms for a sex worker in German; dual use as literal label for prostitutes and as a general sexual insult; slightly less severe than 'Hure' in some regional registers; frequently appears in insult compounds."}
